# EXPECTED root-lane counts for the NEXT lane run — WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE IT RUNS.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (D0A-R21-07). Two consecutive lane runs had a correct figure and a
# WRONG explanation of it: R19-06 (the "+2" named an internal test leg as a second #[test])
# and R20-07 (the "+1" named a test that already existed). The second happened while claiming
# the first had made attribution "checkable". It had not — it had made it more confidently
# phrased.
#
# THE FIX IS COMMIT ORDER, NOT PROSE. A file recording EXPECTED=n in the SAME commit as the
# result is no more auditable than a sentence in a commit message: both are written knowing
# the answer. Only `git log` showing this file's commit STRICTLY BEFORE the result's commit
# establishes that the prediction predates the measurement. That is the entire property.
#
# PROTOCOL
#   1. Derive the expectation from the unprivileged pair and the root-gating of each change.
#   2. Commit THIS FILE ALONE, with the derivation in the message.
#   3. Run the lane.
#   4. Commit the measured pair in `.githooks/runtime-test-count-baseline.root`, SEPARATELY.
#   5. A mismatch is a RESULT, not an error to reconcile — record which side was wrong.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPERSEDED — LANE RUN 11, first expectation (committed 2026-08-29 at d6fb698)
#
#   EXPECTED_EXECUTED=174  EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
#
# NEVER MEASURED, and that is normal rather than a failure. It was derived from an
# unprivileged 154/25; the R21-03 and R21-05 tests then landed and moved the tree to 156/25
# before run 11 happened. The protocol's answer to drift is to RE-DERIVE and re-commit, not
# to adjust the old number — amending it in the same commit as the tests that invalidated it
# would have destroyed the only property this file has, which is that the prediction predates
# the measurement. A reader of `git log` will see a prediction with no result beside it; this
# note is why.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANE RUN 11 — expectation, committed 2026-08-29 at 298d4db, BEFORE the run.
#
# DERIVATION, written so it can be checked rather than believed:
#   run 10 measured           EXECUTED=173 SKIPPED=5   (at unprivileged 153/25)
#   unprivileged is now       EXECUTED=156 SKIPPED=25  (+3 since run 10)
#
#   The +3, each VERIFIED not root-gated (no geteuid check, no SKIP branch, no
#   bwrap_available guard — grepped, not assumed), so each executes at root as well:
#     1. service::tests::a_gate_denied_action_sends_no_preview          (R21-01, socketpair
#        + stub SessionSource)
#     2. action::tests::preview_renders_the_bound_schema_version        (R21-03, pure)
#     3. service::tests::an_oversized_preview_is_denied_before_the_action_is_stored
#        (R21-05, socketpair + stub SessionSource)
#
#   Therefore root gains exactly three: 173 + 3 = 176, and NO skip changes.
#
# The five root skips are unchanged: b1_daemon_binary (needs --features
# insecure-test-seams), live_logind_query (standing DEFER), and three that skip BECAUSE the
# run is privileged (an_unreadable_login_defs, a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused,
# pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier).
#
# IF THE MEASUREMENT DISAGREES, that is a RESULT. Record which side was wrong — the
# derivation above is the thing to check first, since it is the part that can be audited.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=176
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
